{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-6d1d32ab-cc4c-435d-a457-90dd34726b2e","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a3b47da67a65b2f2","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9020-c1vtmcry/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E002.md","content":"# Productize the vLLM ROCm serving runtime for campaign-cleared models\n\n## Description\n\nAn Implementation epic that turns the validated ROCm serving capability into a productized runtime: a vLLM ROCm serving runtime image built in the midstream serving-runtimes repository, the build-pipeline support for it, and the ServingRuntime definition that makes it deployable on AMD Instinct nodes. Which models are enabled is set by the validation campaign's go/no-go outcome — this epic is gated on that resolution and its scope is rewritten to match the cleared model set.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Add a ROCm build variant of the vLLM serving runtime image to the midstream serving-runtimes repository, building on a released upstream ROCm base image and covering the models cleared by the validation campaign.\n- Extend the repository's existing build pipeline to build and release the ROCm image variant alongside the current CUDA builds.\n- Provide the ServingRuntime/ClusterServingRuntime definition that deploys the ROCm vLLM runtime with AMD GPU resource (amd.com/gpu) requests for inference.\n- Verify end-to-end serving through the platform's serving path for the cleared models on AMD Instinct nodes.\n- Ensure existing CUDA-based serving runtimes are unaffected by the change.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The vLLM ROCm serving runtime image builds in the midstream repository and its build pipeline is green, including the repository's Konflux pipeline.\n- A ServingRuntime definition deploys the ROCm vLLM runtime with amd.com/gpu resource requests, and InferenceServices using it serve the campaign-cleared models on AMD Instinct nodes.\n- The set of models enabled by default matches the campaign's go/no-go scope; models that did not clear are not enabled.\n- Existing CUDA-based serving runtimes and inference workloads on NVIDIA hardware show no regression from this change.\n- The ROCm base image and version pinned for the productized runtime are recorded.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-2 (P0): a supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime is productized for the models the validation campaign clears.\n\n## Risks\n\n- Gated on the validation campaign outcome: if only a subset of models clears, productize that subset; if no model clears, this epic is removed and the parity gaps are reported upstream instead of productizing.\n- Upstream ROCm runtime image releases are controlled by AMD and the upstream communities and may not align with the platform's release trains; the pinned base image may need to track the closest released upstream build, which can delay availability in a given train.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":51491,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b885a4284ba31d43","agent_id":"a494e83127aea9e39","session_id":"0cf99ff6-f962-401b-a34e-cfcb3645e2fd","uuid":"0695bd58-595c-4b1f-ba7f-f18d95c0f427","timestamp":"2026-10-26T14:33:59.286Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9020"}
