{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bbe7ceeda5730737","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n3\tepic_count: 5\n4\tcritical_path_length: 3\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\trevised: false\n7\ttriage: null\n8\ttriage_rationale: null\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-9020 (AMD GPU / ROCm enablement for serving and training)\n11\t\n12\tStrategy: RHAISTRAT-9020, priority Major, status Refinement Done.\n13\tTriage: full decomposition (not below-threshold — the strategy spans four\n14\tcomponents, two owning teams, and multiple architecturally distinct work\n15\tstreams: a hardware validation campaign, serving-runtime productization,\n16\ttraining enablement, and documentation; not docs-only — code and\n17\tconfiguration changes are required).\n18\t\n19\t## Epic List\n20\t\n21\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Component | Priority |\n22\t|----|-------|------|------|-----------|----------|\n23\t| RHAISTRAT-9020-E001 | AMD Instinct validation campaign: vLLM ROCm serving parity for the supported model set | Investigation | RHOAI Serving | Serving Runtimes | P0 |\n24\t| RHAISTRAT-9020-E002 | Productize the vLLM ROCm serving runtime for campaign-cleared models | Implementation | RHOAI Serving | Serving Runtimes | P0 |\n25\t| RHAISTRAT-9020-E003 | Enable PyTorch ROCm training for single- and multi-GPU PyTorchJobs | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | Training Operator | P1 |\n26\t| RHAISTRAT-9020-E004 | Kueue amd.com/gpu quota handling for AMD Instinct workloads | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | Distributed Workloads | P1 |\n27\t| RHAISTRAT-9020-E005 | Document AMD GPU (ROCm) support: hardware, drivers, and validated models | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI Docs | Documentation | P1 |\n28\t\n29\t## Dependency DAG\n30\t\n31\t```mermaid\n32\tgraph TD\n33\t    E001[\"E001 — vLLM ROCm serving validation campaign (Investigation, P0)\"]\n34\t    E002[\"E002 — Productize vLLM 