OCm-specific constraints for multi-GPU jobs, for use by documentation and support.\n41\t\n42\t## Acceptance Criteria\n43\t\n44\t- A single-GPU PyTorchJob requesting amd.com/gpu completes a training run successfully on AMD Instinct nodes.\n45\t- A multi-GPU PyTorchJob completes a distributed training run successfully on AMD Instinct nodes with correct multi-worker behavior.\n46\t- Jobs are admitted through Kueue: amd.com/gpu quota is enforced and all-or-nothing admission holds for multi-GPU jobs.\n47\t- The supported PyTorch ROCm runtime basis (image and versions) is defined and recorded.\n48\t\n49\t## HLR Traceability\n50\t\n51\t- HLR-3 (P1): PyTorch training on ROCm is supported for single- and multi-GPU jobs admitted through Kueue, with amd.com/gpu quota handling (job/runtime portion).\n52\t\n53\t## Risks\n54\t\n55\t- Validation requires physical AMD Instinct hardware; node access (procurement or partner lab) is an availability precondition granted outside the strategy and is not an acceptance criterion.\n56\t- PyTorch ROCm image releases are upstream-controlled and may not align with platform release trains.\n57\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bcb39275eab1bbb4","agent_id":"adfc7f6c4d002bec8","session_id":"0cf99ff6-f962-401b-a34e-cfcb3645e2fd","uuid":"91433db8-47da-4d82-ba58-8f2550df3a68","timestamp":"2026-10-26T14:36:34.593Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8b30c9dc814c80bf","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
