g for AMD GPUs.\n45\t- All-or-nothing admission holds: a multi-GPU workload requesting amd.com/gpu is admitted only when its full request can be satisfied.\n46\t- Quota exhaustion behavior is verified: workloads beyond quota remain pending and are admitted when quota is released.\n47\t- Existing NVIDIA GPU quota handling and admitted workloads are unaffected.\n48\t\n49\t## HLR Traceability\n50\t\n51\t- HLR-3 (P1): PyTorch training on ROCm is supported for single- and multi-GPU jobs admitted through Kueue, with amd.com/gpu quota handling (quota/admission portion).\n52\t\n53\t## Risks\n54\t\n55\t- Quota validation on real workloads requires AMD GPU nodes; node access is an availability precondition granted outside the strategy.\n56\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bcb39275eab1bbb4","agent_id":"adfc7f6c4d002bec8","session_id":"0cf99ff6-f962-401b-a34e-cfcb3645e2fd","uuid":"17c9cfdc-54e7-4cfd-bacc-5d26ab704568","timestamp":"2026-10-26T14:36:39.162Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b18ef5a0f86fbfbe","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
