MD GPU sharing/partitioning are out of scope and not implied as supported.\n48\t\n49\t## Acceptance Criteria\n50\t\n51\t- Documentation states the supported AMD hardware and the driver/ROCm prerequisites for both serving and training.\n52\t- Documentation states the validated model list, consistent with the campaign's go/no-go scope and what was productized.\n53\t- Documentation includes the prerequisites and usage notes for PyTorch ROCm training jobs (single- and multi-GPU through Kueue with amd.com/gpu quota).\n54\t- Content is technically reviewed against the implemented capability before publication.\n55\t\n56\t## HLR Traceability\n57\t\n58\t- HLR-4 (P2): documentation states supported AMD hardware, driver prerequisites, and the validated model list. The epic's priority is P1 via the docs-authoring priority exception (strategy frontmatter priority Major → P1).\n59\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-974fd916bfbaa1a8","agent_id":"a6136c4fcc4cf1cc7","session_id":"0cf99ff6-f962-401b-a34e-cfcb3645e2fd","uuid":"5a945118-26c9-4bc7-bbdd-6e0dc191e227","timestamp":"2026-10-26T14:41:49.295Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ad4bc7b5a1062ec5","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
