through Kueue with amd.com/gpu quota\") is an acceptance-criterion gate on the training epic, not a DAG edge. |\n57\t| No konflux-onboarding epic | Rule 20 (inapplicable) | Serving Runtimes is already Konflux-onboarded (architecture context: `serving-runtimes.md`, \"Konflux onboarded: yes\"), and the ROCm image is a new image variant in an existing midstream repo. The pipeline extension is part of E002's scope with a \"build pipeline green\" AC (Rule 25), not a standalone onboarding epic. |\n58\t| No repo-onboarding / license-validation epics | Rule 20 (inapplicable) | All affected components exist in architecture context and have midstream repos; no new component is being provisioned. |\n59\t\n60\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n61\t\n62\t| HLR | Priority | Requirement (abbreviated) | Epic(s) |\n63\t|-----|----------|---------------------------|---------|\n64\t| HLR-1 | P0 | Validation campaign on physical AMD Instinct hardware; functional/performance parity data; go/no-go scope for productization | E001 |\n65\t| HLR-2 | P0 | Supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime productized for cleared models | E002 |\n66\t| HLR-3 | P1 | PyTorch training on ROCm for single-/multi-GPU jobs admitted through Kueue with amd.com/gpu quota handling | E003 (job/runtime side), E004 (quota/admission side) |\n67\t| HLR-4 | P2 | Documentation: supported AMD hardware, driver prerequisites, validated model list | E005 |\n68\t\n69\tFull HLR coverage — no orphaned requirements. HLR-3 splits across two epics\n70\tbecause the job runtime (Training Operator) and the quota/admission layer\n71\t(Distributed Workloads) are different components; both are owned by the\n72\tDistributed Workloads team but rule 1 (different component → separate epics)\n73\tapplies. HLR-4's epic carries P1 (not P2) via the docs-authoring priority\n74\texception: strategy frontmatter priority is Major → P1.\n75\t\n76\t## Open Questions Disposition\n77\t\n78\t| Strategy open question | Disposition | Reasoning |\n79\t|--------------