loyment surface it runs under is exercised within those epics' ACs.\n99\t- No component names were invented or combined; all values are verbatim from\n100\t  `.context/rhai-components.txt` (including \"Documentation\" for the\n101\t  docs-authoring epic).\n102\t\n103\t## Health Warnings\n104\t\n105\t- **Missing strategy sections.** The strategy has no Impacted Teams table, no\n106\t  Dependencies table, no Given/When/Then Acceptance Criteria, and no\n107\t  Non-Functional Requirements. Teams were derived from architecture-context\n108\t  owning teams (KServe/Serving Runtimes → RHOAI Serving; Training\n109\t  Operator/Distributed Workloads → Distributed Workloads). The documentation\n110\t  epic's team (RHOAI Docs) is an assumption — confirm with the strategy author.\n111\t  Epic acceptance criteria were derived from the HLRs, not from strategy-level\n112\t  ACs.\n113\t- **Availability preconditions, not ACs.** Both strategy open questions\n114\t  (hardware access, upstream image cadence) are externally controlled. They\n115\t  are recorded as risks on the affected epics; the ACs sit on engineering\n116\t  deliverables (the campaign report, the productized runtime, the validated\n117\t  training path), per the acceptance-criteria rules.\n118\t- **Docs priority exception.** E005 is P1 (strategy priority Major → P1)\n119\t  although HLR-4 is P2; the docs-authoring epic is exempt from priority\n120\t  inheritance.\n121\t- **Priority inversions.** None found: the P0 campaign gates the P0\n122\t  productization; training and quota work are P1 as their HLR dictates.\n123\t\n124\t## Tiered Delivery\n125\t\n126\tThe external dependency (upstream ROCm image cadence, and AMD hardware\n127\tavailability) has uncertain timing, but the strategy delivers partial value\n128\twithout release-aligned productization:\n129\t\n130\t- **Tier 1 (independent, start immediately)**: E001 validation campaign (runs\n131\t  directly on upstream-published ROCm images), E003 PyTorch ROCm training