{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8e72709d85b6003d","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9020-E002\n3\ttitle: Productize the vLLM ROCm serving runtime for campaign-cleared models\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n5\tcomponent: Serving Runtimes\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9020-E001\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9020-E001\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the campaign clears only a subset of the supported model set,\n15\t    productize only that subset; if no model clears, remove this epic and report the\n16\t    parity gaps upstream instead of productizing.\n17\tai_signals:\n18\t  change_specificity: 0\n19\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n20\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n21\t  existing_foundation: 1\n22\t  open_questions: -1\n23\t  external_dependency: -1\n24\t  human_process_gates: -1\n25\t  repo_access: 1\n26\t  architecture_claims: 1\n27\timplementation_type: null\n28\tinvestigation_signals: null\n29\tai_implementability: Medium\n30\tai_implementability_score: 2\n31\tjira_key: null\n32\tbranch: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Productize the vLLM ROCm serving runtime for campaign-cleared models\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tAn Implementation epic that turns the validated ROCm serving capability into a productized runtime: a vLLM ROCm serving runtime image built in the midstream serving-runtimes repository, the build-pipeline support for it, and the ServingRuntime definition that makes it deployable on AMD Instinct nodes. Which models are enabled is set by the validation campaign's go/no-go outcome — this epic is gated on that resolution and its scope is rewritten to match the cleared model set.\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- Add a ROCm build variant of the vLLM serving runtime image to the midstream serving-runtimes repository, building on a released upstream ROCm base image and covering the models cleared by the validation campaign.\n43\t- Extend the repository's existing build pipeline to build and release the ROCm image variant alongside the current CUDA builds.\n44\t- Provide the ServingRuntime/ClusterServingRuntime definition that deploys the ROCm vLLM runtime with AMD GPU resource (amd.com/gpu) requests for inference.\n45\t- Verify end-to-end serving through the platform's serving path for the cleared models on AMD Instinct nodes.\n46\t- Ensure existing CUDA-based serving runtimes are unaffected by the change.\n47\t\n48\t## Acceptance Criteria\n49\t\n50\t- The vLLM ROCm serving runtime image builds in the midstream repository and its build pipeline is green, including the repository's Konflux pipeline.\n51\t- A ServingRuntime definition deploys the ROCm vLLM runtime with amd.com/gpu resource requests, and InferenceServices using it serve the campaign-cleared models on AMD Instinct nodes.\n52\t- The set of models enabled by default matches the campaign's go/no-go scope; models that did not clear are not enabled.\n53\t- Existing CUDA-based serving runtimes and inference workloads on NVIDIA hardware show no regression from this change.\n54\t- The ROCm base image and version pinned for the productized runtime are recorded.\n55\t\n56\t## HLR Traceability\n57\t\n58\t- HLR-2 (P0): a supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime is productized for the models the validation campaign clears.\n59\t\n60\t## Risks\n61\t\n62\t- Gated on the validation campaign outcome: if only a subset of models clears, productize that subset; if no model clears, this epic is removed and the parity gaps are reported upstream instead of productizing.\n63\t- Upstream ROCm runtime image releases are controlled by AMD and the upstream communities and may not align with the platform's release trains; the pinned base image may need to track the closest released upstream build, which can delay availability in a given train.\n64\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bd0bb8b882efc9cf","agent_id":"a8f1