{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a07255714ba6ec86","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9020-E003\n3\ttitle: Enable PyTorch ROCm training for single- and multi-GPU PyTorchJobs\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n5\tcomponent: Training Operator\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 0\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 0\n15\t  external_dependency: -1\n16\t  human_process_gates: 0\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 3\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Enable PyTorch ROCm training for single- and multi-GPU PyTorchJobs\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tAn Implementation epic making PyTorch training on AMD Instinct accelerators (ROCm) a supported path: PyTorchJob workloads run single- and multi-GPU training on ROCm and are admitted through the platform's queueing system with AMD GPU quota. This epic covers the Training Operator side of that capability — the supported runtime basis for ROCm training jobs and validation of job topologies on AMD GPUs.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Define the supported runtime basis for PyTorch ROCm training jobs (training image, PyTorch ROCm build, and versions), building on upstream-published ROCm support.\n38\t- Enable PyTorchJob worker pods to request and run on AMD GPU resources (amd.com/gpu) in both single-GPU and multi-GPU (multi-worker) topologies.\n39\t- Validate single-GPU and multi-GPU PyTorch training jobs on ROCm on AMD Instinct nodes, including admission through Kueue with amd.com/gpu quota and all-or-nothing gang semantics.\n40\t- Record the supported job shapes and any ROCm-specific constraints for multi-GPU jobs, for use by documentation and support.\n41\t\n42\t## Acceptance Criteria\n43\t\n44\t- A single-GPU PyTorchJob requesting amd.com/gpu completes a training run successfully on AMD Instinct nodes.\n45\t- A multi-GPU PyTorchJob completes a distributed training run successfully on AMD Instinct nodes with correct multi-worker behavior.\n46\t- Jobs are admitted through Kueue: amd.com/gpu quota is enforced and all-or-nothing admission holds for multi-GPU jobs.\n47\t- The supported PyTorch ROCm runtime basis (image and versions) is defined and recorded.\n48\t\n49\t## HLR Traceability\n50\t\n51\t- HLR-3 (P1): PyTorch training on ROCm is supported for single- and multi-GPU jobs admitted through Kueue, with amd.com/gpu quota handling (job/runtime portion).\n52\t\n53\t## Risks\n54\t\n55\t- Validation requires physical AMD Instinct hardware; node access (procurement or partner lab) is an availability precondition granted outside the strategy and is not an acceptance criterion.\n56\t- PyTorch ROCm image releases are upstream-controlled and may not align with platform release trains.\n57\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bd0bb8b882efc9cf","agent_id":"a8f1c7235544b55fc","session_id":"0cf99ff6-f962-401b-a34e-cfcb3645e2fd","uuid":"031fcecd-8c59-4c8a-a757-a34dc036c44b","timestamp":"2026-10-26T14:43:04.992Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a07255714ba6ec86","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
