{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aee4e9371331e371","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9020-E004\n3\ttitle: Kueue amd.com/gpu quota handling for AMD Instinct workloads\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 0\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 0\n15\t  external_dependency: 0\n16\t  human_process_gates: 0\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 4\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Kueue amd.com/gpu quota handling for AMD Instinct workloads\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tAn Implementation epic covering the Distributed Workloads (Kueue) side of AMD GPU enablement: quota and admission handling for the amd.com/gpu resource, so batch AI workloads requesting AMD Instinct accelerators are admitted, quota-accounted, and gang-scheduled like their NVIDIA counterparts.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Extend the queueing configuration to account for amd.com/gpu resources within the ClusterQueue/LocalQueue quota model.\n38\t- Define resource flavors covering AMD GPU nodes so workloads requesting amd.com/gpu are matched and admitted correctly.\n39\t- Validate quota enforcement for amd.com/gpu: admission honors quota limits, and all-or-nothing (waitForPodsReady) admission holds for multi-GPU workloads.\n40\t- Verify the AMD quota path does not disrupt existing NVIDIA GPU quota handling and admission.\n41\t\n42\t## Acceptance Criteria\n43\t\n44\t- Workloads requesting amd.com/gpu are admitted against ClusterQueue/LocalQueue quota with correct resource accounting for AMD GPUs.\n45\t- All-or-nothing admission holds: a multi-GPU workload requesting amd.com/gpu is admitted only when its full request can be satisfied.\n46\t- Quota exhaustion behavior is verified: workloads beyond quota remain pending and are admitted when quota is released.\n47\t- Existing NVIDIA GPU quota handling and admitted workloads are unaffected.\n48\t\n49\t## HLR Traceability\n50\t\n51\t- HLR-3 (P1): PyTorch training on ROCm is supported for single- and multi-GPU jobs admitted through Kueue, with amd.com/gpu quota handling (quota/admission portion).\n52\t\n53\t## Risks\n54\t\n55\t- Quota validation on real workloads requires AMD GPU nodes; node access is an availability precondition granted outside the strategy.\n56\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bd0bb8b882efc9cf","agent_id":"a8f1c7235544b55fc","session_id":"0cf99ff6-f962-401b-a34e-cfcb3645e2fd","uuid":"a2bfe0ad-7256-495d-9655-e8f0d6e691f2","timestamp":"2026-10-26T14:43:07.944Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-aee4e9371331e371","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
